<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">informis</span></b> , e, adj.
		2. in-forma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that has no form</i> or <i>not a
				proper form</i>, <i>unformed</i>, <i>shapeless.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum res muta aut informis fit loquens et
					formata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 53, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alveus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					21, 26, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 15, 13, § 63</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>unshapely</i>, <i>misshapen</i>, <i>deformed</i>, <i>hideous</i>, <i>horrid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cadaver,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 264</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hiemes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 10, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">situs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 2, 2, 118</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nota in ore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 5, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">color,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					4, 4, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">informes sanguine peltae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 12, 528</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imbre cruento informis facies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 224</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					6, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 12, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">letum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 603</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil est illis (metallis) informius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 94</span></i>
			
			<i>med.— Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infor-mĭter</span></b> , <i>hideously</i>, <i>horridly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sonare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 12, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
